---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---
<Base title="AI systems for offices" description="You already pay for Claude, ChatGPT, or Grok. The chat has never seen your files. I build the missing piece on a computer you own, and I train your staff until they use it.">
  <Hero variant="graph" tall eyebrow={`${site.legalName} · ${site.location}`} title="The AI you pay for has never seen your files.">
    <p class="lede">I build AI systems and custom software solutions for offices. Let AI focus on the busywork so you can focus on your business.</p>
    {site.booking && (
      <Fragment slot="actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-book>Book a free consultation</button>
      </Fragment>
    )}
  </Hero>

  <section class="section" id="field-agent">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Customizable solutions</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3><span class="wordmark">Home<span class="accent"> base</span></span></h3>
          <p>A program on a computer at your office, which you own. It files the mail and the scans, drafts the reply, and answers from your own documents, with the page. It uses the Claude, ChatGPT, Grok, or open-source account you already pay for.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3><span class="wordmark">Field<span class="accent"> Agent</span></span></h3>
          <p>The phone app, on iOS and Android. It shows what needs a person today. Ask from the job, and the answer comes from the office files. Nothing changes until someone taps Allow.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Mission support</h3>
          <p>Once it is in, I train your staff on their own work. They learn how to ask, how to check the page, and how to keep a client file out of a personal chat. When the office changes, I change the system with it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-wide">
        <h3>Built to order</h3>
        <p>If what you need is not the system above, I build that instead, around the way you already work. <a href="/software">See custom software</a></p>
      </div>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/map">See the system map</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
